# The skip lines of oracle O6 (plan 5.12.6; section 12, 'M21.c extended'):
# a 'skip O6[@<triple>][:<level>] <test path> <reason>' line of
# msil/utils/equiv-allowed.txt names a test whose msil-ld image has members
# that its -S build lacks by design (plan 5.8.10), so the PEVerify /md
# messages of the image that runs cannot all be the baseline's. msil-verify.py
# --md-baseline with --equiv-skip FILE --test PATH [--triple T] [--level L]
# matches the lines exactly as msil-equiv.py matches O3's and O4's, prints
# 'O6 skipped: <reason>' and does not run O6; O6 is never weakened for any
# other test. b.exe has a metadata message (a literal field without a
# constant, 0x80131B17) that a.exe lacks, so O6 of b.exe against a.exe fails
# wherever it runs (o6-md-baseline.test of ../equiv has the images):
# (1) a 'skip O6' line that names this test (or a directory above it) skips
#     O6, and the run passes;
# (2) lines that do not cover the test leave O6 running, and it still fails
#     on the unexpected message: an O6 line for another test, an O3 line for
#     this test (each line covers its own oracle only), an O6 line for
#     another triple or level, and no --equiv-skip at all;
# (3) a qualified line covers the test for its triple and level only;
# (4) the real equiv-allowed.txt skips O6 of msil/test/M1/07-globals/alias.c
#     and weak-undefined.c (ALIAS address fields, UNDEFINED WEAK zero fields)
#     at every triple and level, and not of msil/test/M1/11-programs/crc32.c,
#     whose O3 line (Windows, -O2) does not reach O6;
# (5) usage errors (status 2): --equiv-skip without --md-baseline, --equiv-skip
#     without --test, and a skip line whose oracle is none of O3, O4 and O6;
# (6) msil-prog.py --equiv-skip under obj still builds the equivalence link
#     when the only line naming the test is an O6 line: O6 lines skip
#     nothing there;
# (7) the composite: a nested lit under msil_pipeline=obj with msil_equiv=1
#     runs the stand-in program of Inputs/nested/refs/o6-c.c; msil-verify
#     gets --equiv-skip <equiv-allowed.txt> --test <the test> --triple
#     <triple> --level O2 before --md-baseline <its -S build>, and O6 runs and
#     passes; with msil_references=<a directory> (M21) O3 also allows the
#     scopes entry ('--allow pinvoke-access --allow scopes').
# REQUIRES: msil-ilasm, msil-ilverify, msil-peverify

# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t
# RUN: %ilasm -exe -output=%t/a.exe %t/a.il
# RUN: %ilasm -exe -output=%t/b.exe %t/b.il
# RUN: %{harness_check} write %t/o6-qualified.txt "skip O6@%msil_triple:O2 msil/test/harness/prog/o6-skip.test this triple at -O2"

# (1)
